  <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The cellular developmental process in which a relatively unspecialized cell, e.g. embryonic or regenerative cell, acquires specialized structural and/or functional features that characterize a specific cell. Differentiation includes the processes involved in commitment of a cell to a specific fate and its subsequent development to the mature state.</obo:IAO_0000115>
