  <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Progression of the exocrine system over time, from its formation to a mature structure. The exocrine system is a system of hormones and glands, where the glands secrete straight to a target site via ducts or tubes. The human exocrine system includes the salivary glands, sweat glands and many glands of the digestive system.</obo:IAO_0000115>
