  <obo:IAO_0000111 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">biological_process</obo:IAO_0000111>
  <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A biological process is the execution of a genetically-encoded biological module or program. It consists of all the steps required to achieve the specific biological objective of the module. A biological process is accomplished by a particular set of molecular functions carried out by specific gene products (or macromolecular complexes), often in a highly regulated manner and in a particular temporal sequence.</obo:IAO_0000115>
