  <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Vertebrate muscle is categorized into three major muscle types defined by their structural and functional properties: skeletal, cardiac and smooth. In Dmel the counterparts are somatic, heart/cardiac and visceral. Here we take a cell type based approach.</rdfs:comment>
