  <oboI:id rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UBERON:0002298</oboI:id>
  <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">'brainstem' is a loose term that sometimes refers to the ventral parts o the brain except for any part of the telencephalon - sometimes it includes the diencephalon or subpallial telencephalon structures (ISBN:0471888893). Here we use it in a more restriced sense, to include only the medulla oblongata, pons (when present) and the midbrain tegmentum (following the ZFA definitions).</rdfs:comment>
