  <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">An organic group formed by removing one or more hydroxy groups from an oxoacid that has the general structure R&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;&lt;em&gt;k&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt;E(=O)&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;&lt;em&gt;l&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt;(OH)&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;&lt;em&gt;m&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt; (&lt;em&gt;l&lt;/em&gt; ≠ 0). Although the term is almost always applied to organic compounds, with carboxylic acid as the oxoacid, acyl groups can in principle be derived from other types of acids such as sulfonic acids or phosphonic acids.</obo:IAO_0000115>
  <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">An organic group formed by removing one or more hydroxy groups from an oxoacid that has the general structure RkE(=O)l(OH)m (l =/= 0). Although the term is almost always applied to organic compounds, with carboxylic acid as the oxoacid, acyl groups can in principle be derived from other types of acids such as sulfonic acids or phosphonic acids.</obo:IAO_0000115>
  <oboI:hasExactSynonym rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">acyl group</oboI:hasExactSynonym>
  <oboI:hasExactSynonym rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">alkanoyl</oboI:hasExactSynonym>
  <oboI:hasOBONamespace rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">chebi_ontology</oboI:hasOBONamespace>
  <oboI:hasRelatedSynonym rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">acyl group</oboI:hasRelatedSynonym>
  <oboI:hasRelatedSynonym rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">acyl groups</oboI:hasRelatedSynonym>
  <oboI:hasRelatedSynonym rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">alkanoyl</oboI:hasRelatedSynonym>
  <oboI:hasRelatedSynonym rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">alkanoyl group</oboI:hasRelatedSynonym>
  <oboI:hasRelatedSynonym rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">groupe acyle</oboI:hasRelatedSynonym>
  <oboI:id rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CHEBI:22221</oboI:id>
  <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">acyl group</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

