  <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The process in which the anatomical structures of the epidermis are generated and organized. The epidermis is the outer epithelial layer of an animal, it may be a single layer that produces an extracellular material (e.g. the cuticle of arthropods) or a complex stratified squamous epithelium, as in the case of many vertebrate species.</obo:IAO_0000115>
  <oboI:hasOBONamespace rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">biological_process</oboI:hasOBONamespace>
  <oboI:hasRelatedSynonym rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">hypodermis morphogenesis</oboI:hasRelatedSynonym>
