  <x_1.1:description xml:lang="en">A material entity that has one or more pathological disorders as parts; which disorders compose one disease is fixed by the diagnostic classification assigned to them, not by an intrinsic unity criterion. Identity is grounded in the continuity of the disorder lineage, not in momentary material composition (cf. a river persisting through complete material replacement).</x_1.1:description>
