  <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A mitotic cell cycle process comprising the steps by which the nucleus of a eukaryotic cell divides; the process involves condensation of chromosomal DNA into a highly compacted form. Canonically, mitosis produces two daughter nuclei whose chromosome complement is identical to that of the mother cell.</obo:IAO_0000115>
