  <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The process in which the anatomical structures of the ascending aorta are generated and organized. The ascending aorta is the portion of the aorta in a two-pass circulatory system that lies between the heart and the arch of aorta. In a two-pass circulatory system blood passes twice through the heart to supply the body once.</obo:IAO_0000115>
