  <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Alternate def: A synovial sheath is a layer of a tendon sheath containing tendons in the hand and foot. They lie internal to the fibrous tendon sheaths. An example is the common synovial sheath for the flexor tendons. [Wikipedia:Synovial_sheath]</rdfs:comment>
