  <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The directed movement of an organic hydroxy compound (organic alcohol) into, out of or within a cell, or between cells, by means of some agent such as a transporter or pore. An organic hydroxy compound is an organic compound having at least one hydroxy group attached to a carbon atom.</obo:IAO_0000115>
