  <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The progression of the heart rudiment over time, from its initial formation to the mature structure. The heart rudiment is a cone-like structure that is formed when myocardial progenitor cells of the heart field fuse at the midline. The heart rudiment is the first structure of the heart tube.</owl:annotatedTarget>
