  <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The progression of a cardiac cushion over time, from its initial formation to the mature structure. The endocardial cushion is a specialized region of mesenchymal cells that will give rise to the heart septa and valves.</owl:annotatedTarget>
  <oboI:hasDbXref rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GOC:mtg_heart</oboI:hasDbXref>
