  <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A flat, squamous-like epithelial cell of mesodermal origin. It forms the mesothelium, which lines the body's serous cavities including the pleural, peritoneal, and pericardial spaces. This cell plays a crucial role in synthesizing and secreting lubricants, such as glycosaminoglycans and surfactants, which minimize friction between adjacent tissues during movement.</owl:annotatedTarget>
