  <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The directed movement of a monoatomic ion into, out of or within a cell, or between cells, by means of some agent such as a transporter or pore. Monatomic ions (also called simple ions) are ions consisting of exactly one atom.</owl:annotatedTarget>
  <oboI:hasDbXref rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GOC:ai</oboI:hasDbXref>
