  <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The process in which a relatively unspecialized cell acquires specialized features of a glandular epithelial cell. A glandular epithelial cell is a columnar/cuboidal epithelial cell found in a two dimensional sheet with a free surface exposed to the lumen of a gland.</owl:annotatedTarget>
  <oboI:hasDbXref rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GOC:dph</oboI:hasDbXref>
