  <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">An endothelial cell comprises the outermost layer or lining of anatomical structures and can be squamous or cuboidal. In mammals, endothelial cell has vimentin filaments and is derived from the mesoderm.</owl:annotatedTarget>
