  <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The process whose specific outcome is the progression of the brain over time, from its formation to the mature structure. Brain development begins with patterning events in the neural tube and ends with the mature structure that is the center of thought and emotion. The brain is responsible for the coordination and control of bodily activities and the interpretation of information from the senses (sight, hearing, smell, etc.).</owl:annotatedTarget>
