  <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A gland that secretes products (excluding hormones and other chemical messengers) into ducts (duct glands) which lead directly into the external environment[WP]. Typical exocrine glands include sweat glands, salivary glands, mammary glands, stomach, liver, pancreas.</owl:annotatedTarget>
  <oboI:hasDbXref rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Wikipedia:Exocrine_gland</oboI:hasDbXref>
